  crises:
  - id: angin_monsun
    eras: 01000000
    triggerYear: 0
    triggerEvent: 
    nameMs: Angin Monsun Berubah
    nameEn: The Monsoon Winds Shift
    descriptionMs: Angin peralihan monsun datang lewat tahun ini. Armada dari Gujerat
      dan China tertahan dan gudang mula penuh.
    descriptionEn: The inter-monsoon winds turn late this year. Fleets from Gujarat
      and China are delayed and warehouses fill up.
    defaultChoice: 0
    choices:
    - id: tunggu
      nameMs: Tunggu angin
      nameEn: Wait for the winds
      descriptionMs: Tiada kos, tetapi eksport perlahan lebih lama.
      descriptionEn: No cost, but exports stay slow for longer.
      cost: 0
    - id: gudang
      nameMs: Simpan dagangan di gudang
      nameEn: Hold cargo in warehouses
      descriptionMs: Bayar sewa gudang supaya dagangan tidak rosak; pedagang berpuas
        hati.
      descriptionEn: Pay for storage so cargo does not spoil; merchants are pleased.
      cost: 400
    - id: jurumudi
      nameMs: Upah jurumudi tempatan
      nameEn: Hire local pilots
      descriptionMs: Jurumudi Orang Laut membawa kapal melalui angin lemah. Ilmu
        pelayaran bertambah.
      descriptionEn: Orang Laut pilots guide ships through the slack winds. Seamanship
        knowledge grows.
      cost: 250
  - id: bah_besar
    eras: 02000000
    triggerYear: 1926
    triggerEvent: 
    nameMs: Bah Besar 1926
    nameEn: The Great Flood of 1926
    descriptionMs: "Pada akhir Disember 1926 hujan luar biasa (dikaitkan dengan La
      Ni\xF1a) membanjiri Pahang, Kelantan, Terengganu, Perak dan Selangor. Penebangan
      hutan untuk estet dan lombong memburukkan banjir."
    descriptionEn: "In late December 1926 extraordinary rains (linked to La Ni\xF1a)
      flood Pahang, Kelantan, Terengganu, Perak and Selangor. Forest clearing for
      estates and mines made the floods worse."
    defaultChoice: 2
    choices:
    - id: bantuan
      nameMs: Dapur bantuan & pemindahan
      nameEn: Relief kitchens and evacuation
      descriptionMs: Lindungi rakyat; kebahagiaan pulih dengan cepat.
      descriptionEn: Protect the people; happiness recovers quickly.
      cost: 2000
    - id: tebatan
      nameMs: Bina semula tebatan & parit
      nameEn: Rebuild bunds and drains
      descriptionMs: Pemulihan lebih pantas; pengeluaran kembali normal.
      descriptionEn: Faster recovery; production returns to normal.
      cost: 3500
    - id: biarkan
      nameMs: Biarkan daerah pulih sendiri
      nameEn: Leave the districts to recover
      descriptionMs: Tiada kos, tetapi pengeluaran dan semangat rakyat merosot.
      descriptionEn: No cost, but output and morale suffer.
      cost: 0
  - id: kemelesetan_1930
    eras: 02000000
    triggerYear: 0
    triggerEvent: kemelesetan_besar
    nameMs: 'Kemelesetan: Kejatuhan Harga Komoditi'
    nameEn: 'Depression: the Commodity Crash'
    descriptionMs: Harga timah dan getah runtuh. Pada 1 Mac 1931 Tanah Melayu, Bolivia,
      Hindia Timur Belanda dan Nigeria memulakan Skim Kawalan Timah Antarabangsa
      untuk menyekat pengeluaran.
    descriptionEn: Tin and rubber prices collapse. On 1 March 1931 British Malaya,
      Bolivia, the Netherlands East Indies and Nigeria begin the International Tin
      Control Scheme to restrict output.
    defaultChoice: 2
    choices:
    - id: kuota
      nameMs: Sertai skim sekatan pengeluaran
      nameEn: Join the output-restriction scheme
      descriptionMs: Harga timah dan getah disokong, tetapi pengeluaran dihadkan.
      descriptionEn: Tin and rubber prices are propped up, but output is capped.
      cost: 0
    - id: kerja_awam
      nameMs: Kerja awam & bantuan
      nameEn: Public works and relief
      descriptionMs: Belanja untuk jalan dan bantuan; rakyat lebih tenang.
      descriptionEn: Spend on roads and relief; the people stay calm.
      cost: 3000
    - id: jimat
      nameMs: Berjimat cermat
      nameEn: Austerity
      descriptionMs: Potong perbelanjaan untuk menambah tabung, tetapi rakyat menderita.
      descriptionEn: Cut spending to rebuild the treasury, but people suffer.
      cost: 0
  - id: krisis_timah
    eras: 03000000
    triggerYear: 0
    triggerEvent: krisis_timah_1985
    nameMs: Keruntuhan Pasaran Timah 1985
    nameEn: The 1985 Tin Market Collapse
    descriptionMs: Pada 24 Oktober 1985 Majlis Timah Antarabangsa gagal membayar
      hutangnya dan Bursa Logam London menggantung dagangan timah. Malaysia menutup
      hampir separuh lombongnya.
    descriptionEn: On 24 October 1985 the International Tin Council defaults on its
      debts and the London Metal Exchange suspends tin trading. Malaysia closes nearly
      half its mines.
    defaultChoice: 2
    choices:
    - id: pelbagai
      nameMs: Pelbagaikan ke perkilangan
      nameEn: Diversify into manufacturing
      descriptionMs: Latih semula pelombong untuk kilang elektronik.
      descriptionEn: Retrain miners for electronics plants.
      cost: 8000
    - id: selamatkan
      nameMs: Selamatkan pelombong
      nameEn: Bail out the miners
      descriptionMs: Subsidi menyokong harga timah tempatan untuk sementara.
      descriptionEn: Subsidies prop up local tin prices for a while.
      cost: 12000
    - id: pasaran
      nameMs: Biarkan pasaran menyesuaikan diri
      nameEn: Let the market adjust
      descriptionMs: Tiada kos; bandar timah merana.
      descriptionEn: No cost; tin towns suffer.
      cost: 0
  - id: krisis_kewangan
    eras: 04000000
    triggerYear: 0
    triggerEvent: krisis_asia_1997
    nameMs: Krisis Kewangan Asia 1997
    nameEn: The 1997 Asian Financial Crisis
    descriptionMs: Ringgit menjunam dan modal asing lari. Pada 1 September 1998 Malaysia
      memperkenalkan kawalan modal terpilih dan memaku ringgit pada RM3.80 se-USD
      (dimansuhkan 2005).
    descriptionEn: The ringgit plunges and foreign capital flees. On 1 September
      1998 Malaysia introduces selective capital controls and pegs the ringgit at
      RM3.80 per US dollar (dropped in 2005).
    defaultChoice: 0
    choices:
    - id: kawalan
      nameMs: Kawalan modal & tambatan ringgit
      nameEn: Capital controls and a ringgit peg
      descriptionMs: Kestabilan pulih, tetapi rakan Barat kurang senang.
      descriptionEn: Stability returns, but Western partners are uneasy.
      cost: 0
    - id: imf
      nameMs: Pakej penjimatan gaya IMF
      nameEn: IMF-style austerity
      descriptionMs: Kadar faedah tinggi dan potongan belanja; pelabur Barat lega.
      descriptionEn: High interest rates and spending cuts; Western investors relax.
      cost: 0
    - id: rangsangan
      nameMs: Rangsangan fiskal
      nameEn: Fiscal stimulus
      descriptionMs: Belanja besar untuk projek awam memastikan pekerjaan.
      descriptionEn: Big public spending keeps people in work.
      cost: 40000
